# YITP Navigation Reference

This document captures every navigation surface currently active in the Youth Impact Training Programme (YITP) project as of the latest commit. All URLs are listed exactly as referenced in the templates so product, QA, and engineering teams can trace how each role experiences the system.

## 1. Public (Desktop) Navigation

Rendered from `templates/unified/navigation.html` and included by every base template (`unified/base.html`, `yitp/base.html`, `yitp/baseprofile.html`, `lms/base.html`).

### 1.1 Primary Links (always visible on desktop)

| Label | URL helper | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Home (logo link) | `{% url 'yitp:home' %}` | Main landing page via the logo at the far-left. |
| Blogs & News | `{% url 'blogapp:blog-list' %}` | Navigation item with active state tied to `blog-list`. |
| Events | `{% url 'events:event_list' %}` | Navigation item with active state tied to `event_list`. |

### 1.2 Language Selector (desktop)

Dropdown button (`.yitp-language-selector`) with options:

| Language | Data attribute |
| --- | --- |
| English | `data-lang="en"` |
| Swahili (Kiswahili) | `data-lang="sw"` |
| Arabic (العربية) | `data-lang="ar"` |
| Africana (Afrikaans) | `data-lang="af"` |
| French (Français) | `data-lang="fr"` |

Each option updates the frontend Google Translate integration (`static/js/yitp-translate-basic.js`).

### 1.3 Authentication Area (desktop)

- **Anonymous visitors** see a single CTA: `Login` → `{% url 'login' %}`. (Additional buttons were pruned earlier to make space for language selector.)
- **Authenticated users** see a dropdown anchored to the avatar chips. Menu items vary by role (see Sections 4–7).

## 2. Mobile Navigation Drawer

Triggered via the hamburger icon (`#sidebar-toggle`). Lives inside the same template block.

### 2.1 Language Grid

Repeats the five languages from Section 1.2. Buttons use the same `data-lang` attributes.

### 2.2 Authenticated Mobile Links

Structured as `.mobile__auth-menu` with conditional logic:

| Role condition | Menu entries |
| --- | --- |
| `user.is_superuser` | `Admin Dashboard` → `{% url 'users:superuser_dashboard' %}`, `Create User` → `{% url 'users:superuser_create_user' %}` |
| `instructor_profile.is_active` and `instructor_role == 'accountant'` | `Finance Dashboard` → `{% url 'users:accountant_dashboard' %}` |
| `instructor_profile.is_active` and `instructor_role == 'content_manager'` | `Content Dashboard` → `{% url 'users:content_manager_dashboard' %}` |
| `instructor_profile.is_active` and any other role (default instructor) | `Instructor Dashboard` → `{% url 'users:instructor_dashboard' %}` |
| No special role | `My Profile` → `{% url 'profile' %}` |
| Shared for everyone | `Programs` → `{% url 'yitp:registration' %}`, `Logout` → `{% url 'logout' %}` |

### 2.3 Anonymous Mobile Buttons

| Label | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Login | `{% url 'login' %}` |
| Sign Up | `{% url 'register' %}` |
| Contact Us | `{% url 'yitp:contact' %}` |

## 3. Profile Navigation (Authenticated Students / Participants)

There is no separate profile navbar; instead, the authenticated dropdown in Section 1.3 exposes contextual entries based on the user’s role.

### 3.1 Base Authenticated Menu (non staff/instructor)

| Order | Label | URL |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Profile Overview | `{% url 'profile' %}` |
| 2 | My Courses | `{% url 'profile' %}?section=courses` |
| 3 | Analytics | `{% url 'profile' %}?section=analytics` |
| 4 | Billing | `{% url 'profile' %}?section=billing` |
| 5 | Account Settings | `{% url 'profile' %}?section=settings` |
| 6 | Achievements | `{% url 'progress:achievements' %}` |
| 7 | Logout | `{% url 'logout' %}` (listed after a divider) |

### 3.2 LMS Entry Points for Students

Although the navigation template is shared, LMS-specific dashboards are exposed through:

- `My Courses` (see above) → internal section switching.
- Deep links from elsewhere (e.g., `courses:my_courses`, `progress:*`) rely on page content rather than nav.

