## 8. LMS Navigation

All LMS templates currently extend `unified/base.html`, so they reuse the public navigation. Additional LMS-specific access points come from page content (sidebars, tabs) rather than the global navbar. Key routes surfaced elsewhere:

| Feature | URL |
| --- | --- |
| LMS Dashboard | `{% url 'courses:dashboard' %}` |
| My Courses | `{% url 'courses:my_courses' %}` |
| Progress Dashboard | `{% url 'progress:dashboard' %}` |
| Achievements | `{% url 'progress:achievements' %}` |
| Communication Hub | `{% url 'communication:dashboard' %}` |

While not visible as top-level nav buttons, these routes are referenced throughout LMS templates (`templates/lms/*`) and from the authenticated dropdown (Achievements) and page content.

## 9. Additional Notes

- **Notifications:** `templates/unified/base.html` includes `includes/notifications.html` immediately after the navbar for all contexts. Indicators within the nav rely on the same data.
- **Sticky behavior:** The nav writes CSS variables (`--header-sticky-offset`) via inline script to keep page content from jumping when the header becomes fixed.
- **CTA buttons removed:** Only a Login button is rendered for anonymous users on desktop; mobile retains Login, Sign Up, and Contact Us.

This document should be updated whenever a new role, menu item, or base template modifies the navigation include.
